&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Talent Acquisition Business Partner Senior Executive will support end-to-end hiring activities and daily people operations to ensure efficient recruitment processes and smooth employee experience across assigned teams while acting as a trusted advisor to business leaders. The position will focus on recruitment delivery, HR coordination, employee operations, and day-to-day people support, while working closely with TA Manager and Head of People to support business and organizational needs.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Acquisition: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full-cycle recruitment process for assigned roles, from sourcing, screening, interviewing, to offer management and onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute sourcing strategies to attract top talent through job boards, social media, referrals, networking, and headhunting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage candidate experience to ensure positive candidate outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using standardized screening techniques, assess the skills, qualifications, and experience of potential candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure an excellent candidate experience throughout the hiring journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Hiring Managers on best hiring practices and decisions, advise stakeholders on talent market insights, hiring trends, and candidate availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the HR &amp;amp; Communications Team to organize engagement activities and develop materials for employer branding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the onboarding process and contribute to improving employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the departments as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Partner:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating with the Head of People in executing people initiatives and day-to-day HR partnering activities across assigned departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as HR PIC for assigned departments on daily people-related matters, supporting the full employee lifecycle from hire to retire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and coordinate performance review cycles, including timeline tracking and process communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent and fair application of policies and practices, balancing business needs with employee experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support managers on operational people matters including attendance follow-up, employee concerns, and team coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare talent reports, workforce data, and people insights for business reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad-hoc HR projects and operational tasks assigned by the People team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree is required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of working experience in the full life cycle of recruitment, TABP is a must, and experience in the Digital Marketing, E-commerce industry is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in HR generalist, People Partner role is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong in utilizing social media platforms (LinkedIn, Facebook, etc.) to drive networking and candidate pool development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coordination and communication skills with ability to work across multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of recruitment best practices, labor market trends, and employer branding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong growth-mindset&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Result-driven and have a good sense of responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good command of English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love It&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance Review (2 times per year)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance Bonus&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
